 ## Overview
-VoISDF is a neural volume rendering method that models volume density as a transformed function of a learned Signed Distance Function (SDF) to improve geometry reconstruction and enable adaptive sampling [S3, unofficial]. Unlike prior methods that extract geometry from an arbitrary level set of a generic density MLP, VoISDF extracts the surface as the zero level-set of the learned SDF, providing a well-defined surface and inductive bias [S3, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from NeRF by using a single density network and error-bound-based adaptive sampling, avoiding the salt-and-pepper artifacts of random sampling and the density mismatch issues of using a second network for inverse CDF sampling [S3, unofficial].
+VoISDF is a neural volume rendering method that models volume density as a transformed function of a learned Signed Distance Function (SDF) to improve geometry reconstruction and enable adaptive sampling [S3, unofficial]. Unlike prior methods that model geometry as a function of density or use random sampling, VoISDF extracts the surface as the zero level-set of the learned SDF and employs an error-bound-driven adaptive sampling algorithm to avoid salt-and-pepper artifacts without requiring a second network [S3, unofficial].
 
